  <reporting-org ref="47045" secondary-reporter="0" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing the TB burden in Lao PDR - Lao (Peoples Democratic Republic) (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The World Health Organization (WHO) estimated the prevalence and incidence of tuberculosis (TB) in Lao PDR in all forms to be 289/100,000 and 151/100,000 respectively. The goal of this Program is to reduce TB prevalence and mortality by half by 2015 relative to 1990, contributing to the achievement of the overall Millennium Development Goals (MDGs). The Programs four objectives are: ensuring universal and equitable access to TB diagnosis and treatment for all people suffering from TB; considerably scaling up programmatic management of drug-resistant TB (PMDT); strengthening TB-HIV collaborative activities; and strengthening managerial capacity of the National TB Program (NTP) and partners. Its target groups include all TB patients, contacts of TB patients, people living with HIV and AIDS (PLHIV) and ethnic minority groups. This is a consolidation of Round 10 and Round 7 TB grants.</narrative>
  </description>
